* MY_LIB original Oasistek LED electrical approximation from datasheets only.
* No manufacturer SPICE model was used. External pin order: 1=K, 2=A.
* Component-specific ISvalue/Nvalue/RSvalue must be passed by Excel/DbLib.
* Fit/calibration is at +25 C, normally 1..25mA. See parameter provenance.
* Six components have only one VFtyp point at20mA: N=2 and RS=0 are assumed.
* Three components use digitized manufacturer typical curves, not measurements.
* This model does not model emitted light, heating, current/power limits,
* luminous intensity, spectra, tolerances, aging, capacitance or recovery time.
* CJO=0 TT=0 explicitly disable unknown dynamics, not a measured-zero claim.
* BV is omitted: the5V reverse rating is NOT a measured breakdown voltage.
* IS is a forward-fit coefficient, NOT a measured reverse leakage current.
* Dforward TEMP=25 fixes this electrical junction at25C even when global
* TEMP differs. No actual LED temperature dependence or self-heating modeled.
* EG=0 XTI=0 are explicit; with fixed device TEMP they do not calibrate a T law.
* Numerical implementation: native tests did not retain tiny direct MODEL IS.
* MODEL IS is
* therefore fixed1e-28 and diodeAREA=ISvalue/1e-28 produces fitted effectiveIS.
* AREA is numerical scaling, NOT physical die area. NativeAREA also divides
* modelRS, so modelRS=RSvalue*AREA preserves the original fitted effectiveRS.
* Fitted targets/parameters are unchanged; no voltage offset or added R used.
* Defaults give an illustrative2.0V@20mA single-point curve, not a specificMPN.
.SUBCKT MY_LIB_LED_DS 1 2 PARAMS: ISvalue=2.49764743936e-19 Nvalue=2 RSvalue=0
Dforward 2 1 DLED {ISvalue/1e-28} TEMP=25
.MODEL DLED D (IS=1e-28 N={Nvalue} RS={RSvalue*ISvalue/1e-28} TNOM=25
+ EG=0 XTI=0 CJO=0 TT=0)
.ENDS MY_LIB_LED_DS
